 ## Overview
-Deferred Filtering Architecture for Compressed Volumes is a specialized rendering pipeline that performs high-quality shading of massive datasets by coordinating visibility- and resolution-aware adaptive data loading with GPU-accelerated per-frame decompression, deblocking, and rendering [S1, S3, unofficial]. It solves the problem of high storage, computation, and transmission overhead associated with massive volume datasets by keeping data in compressed format at all stages except during transient local reconstruction, thereby minimizing data transfer between main memory and GPU memory [S1, S3, unofficial]. It differs from [Stripe-based On-the-fly Decoding](5363-stripe-based-on-the-fly-decoding.md) and [CPU-Based Block Decompression](7197-cpu-based-block-decompression.md) by performing the reconstruction entirely within the GPU's texture hardware pipeline via dependent fetches and a multi-pass deferred approach, allowing for post-process deblocking without modifying the encoding method [S1, S3, unofficial].
+Deferred Filtering Architecture for Compressed Volumes is a specialized rendering pipeline that performs high-quality shading of massive datasets by coordinating visibility- and resolution-aware adaptive data loading with GPU-accelerated per-frame decompression, deblocking, and rendering [S1, S3, unofficial]. It solves the problem of high storage, computation, and transmission overhead associated with massive volume datasets by keeping data in compressed format at all stages except during transient local reconstruction, thereby minimizing data transfer between main memory and GPU memory [S1, S3, unofficial]. It differs from prior single-resolution slice-based methods by generalizing deferred filtering to multi-resolution settings combining levels of detail with adaptive loading and visibility culling [S1, S3, unofficial]. It differs from in-loop deblocking by using a post-loop approach that does not require modification of the encoding method and supports multiple encoding methods [S1, S3, unofficial].
 
